\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, I was blind! I could not see
\par In  Thy marred visage any grace;
\par But now the beauty of Thy face
\par In radiant vision dawns on me.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lord, I was deaf! I could not hear
\par The thrilling music of Thy voice;
\par But now I hear Thee and rejoice,
\par And all Thine uttered words are dear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lord, I was dumb! I could not speak
\par The grace and glory of Thy name;
\par But now, as touched with living flame,
\par My lips Thine eager praises wake.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Lord, I was dead! I could not stir
\par My lifeless soul to come to Thee;
\par But now, since Thou hast quickened me,
\par I rise from sin's dark sepulchre.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. For Thou  hast made the blind to see,
\par The deaf to hear, the dumb to speak,
\par The dead to live, and lo, I break
\par The chains of my captivity!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

